<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Steering Vector Plots</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Illegitimate Self-Preference</h3>

<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03647v1/bias.svg" id="A1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:357/255;" width="357" height="255"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Probability of the self-evaluating model <math id="A1.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> choosing the comparison model <math id="A1.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>’s summary on the y-axis, and multipliers on the x-axis. This plot is for the subset of examples in which <math id="A1.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> thinks its summary is better and the gold judges <math id="A1.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> think that <math id="A1.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>’s summary is better.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Unbiased Agreement</h3>

<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03647v1/agreement.svg" id="A1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:357/255;" width="357" height="255"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Probability of the self-evaluating model <math id="A1.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> choosing the comparison model <math id="A1.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>’s summary on the y-axis. This plot is for the subset of examples in which <math id="A1.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> agrees with the gold judges <math id="A1.F3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A1.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>’s summary is best. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Legitimate Self-Preference</h3>

<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03647v1/lsp.svg" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:357/255;" width="357" height="255"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Probability of the self-evaluating model <math id="A1.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> choosing its own summary on the y-axis, and multipliers on the x-axis. This plot is for the subset of examples in which the self-evaluating model <math id="A1.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> thinks that its summary is better and the gold judges <math id="A1.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G_{1},\dots,G_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> agree. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Optimization Parameters</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our experiments, we froze the model weights, hooked an additive vector, and optimized over the top 20th percentile of prompts based on the highest probability that <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> would select its own answer, given that the gold label votes for model <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, maximizing the probability of target completion <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to model <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>’s response and minimizing the initial, biased completion <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=v_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=v_{J}</annotation></semantics></math>. We optimize using <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adam</span> on layer 14 of <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama-3.1-8b-instruct</span> for 20 iterations with a learning rate of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Prompts</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Pairwise Evaluation Prompts</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.1 </span>Unaware Setting</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="82.44" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 82.44" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,82.44) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3B0A4;" fill="#F3B0A4" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 12.92 L 0 69.52 C 0 76.65 5.78 82.44 12.92 82.44 L 464.46 82.44 C 471.59 82.44 477.38 76.65 477.38 69.52 L 477.38 12.92 C 477.38 5.78 471.59 0 464.46 0 L 12.92 0 C 5.78 0 0 5.78 0 12.92 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FEF6F4;" fill="#FEF6F4" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 12.92 L 1.11 60.16 L 476.27 60.16 L 476.27 12.92 C 476.27 6.39 470.98 1.11 464.46 1.11 L 12.92 1.11 C 6.39 1.11 1.11 6.39 1.11 12.92 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.92 67.9)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:28.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.18" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="392.56"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
